{"name":"Mistletoe Whisper","hex":"#5a8065","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mistletoe","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of numerous hemiparasitic evergreen plants of the order Santalales with white berries that grow in the crowns of apple trees, oaks, and other trees, such as the European mistletoe (Viscum album) and American mistletoe or eastern mistletoe (Phoradendron leucarpum).","A sprig of one such plant used as a Christmas decoration, associated with the custom that a man may kiss any woman standing beneath it."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mistletoe"},{"term":"whisper","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of speaking in a quiet voice, especially without vibration of the vocal cords; the sound thus produced.","A rumor."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To speak softly or under one's breath, so as to be heard only by one near at hand; to utter words without sonant breath; to talk without that vibration of the vocal cords which gives sonorous, or vocal, sound.","To say (something) softly or under one's breath, so as to be heard only by one near at hand; to utter (something) without sonant breath, without that vibration of the vocal cords which gives sonorous, or vocal, sound."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whisper"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mistletoe","blocks":[{"text":"Mistletoe is the common name for obligate hemiparasitic plants in the order Santalales. They are attached to their host tree or shrub by a structure called the haustorium, through which they extract water and nutrients from the host plant. There are hundreds of species which mostly live in tropical regions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Viscum_album_2026_G1.jpg/330px-Viscum_album_2026_G1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mistletoe","wikidata":"Q2885646"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thum